========================================================================================================================
HPE VM ESSENTIALS (VME) - ALL-NODE NFS DATASTORE TROUBLESHOOTING
========================================================================================================================

1. ALL-NODE PARALLEL DIAGNOSTICS (Run using cluster-shell or on each node individually)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CATEGORY               COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Mount Verification     mount -t nfs4                                   List all active NFSv4 mount attachments on the node
Mount Verification     cat /proc/mounts | grep -i nfs                  Bypass hanging 'df -h' to read kernel-level mounts
Mount Verification     sudo nfsstat -m                                 Display active mount options, flags, and variations

Network & Ports        nc -zv <NFS_Server_IP> 2049                     Verify direct TCP communication to the NFS daemon
Network & Ports        rpcinfo -p <NFS_Server_IP>                     Query remote RPC portmapper (checks ports 111, 20048)
Network & Ports        showmount -e <NFS_Server_IP>                    Query the storage target for exposed export subpaths

Performance & Latency  sudo nfsstat -rc                                Check RPC client execution timeout/retry counters
Performance & Latency  sudo tcpdump -i any port 2049 -n                Sniff active NFS storage transactions and retransmissions

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. EMERGENCY PROCEDURES FOR STUCK/FROZEN NFS DATASTORES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ACTION                 COMMAND                                         DESCRIPTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Lazy Unmount           sudo umount -l /mnt/<nfs_mount_point>           Instantly detach a hanging NFS path from directory tree
Force Unmount          sudo umount -f /mnt/<nfs_mount_point>           Forcefully drop mount point (May hang if IO is locked)
Remount Datastore      sudo mount -a                                   Force OS to re-read fstab profiles and remount paths

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. KVM / LIBVIRT LAYER SYNCHRONIZATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KVM Pool Check         sudo virsh pool-list --all                      Verify status of KVM-managed storage definitions
KVM Pool Check         sudo virsh pool-info <nfs_pool_name>            Display overall capacity and allocation state of pool
KVM Pool Check         sudo virsh pool-refresh <nfs_pool_name>         Force libvirt to scan filesystem for new QCOW2/ISOs
